  "description": "Whether you’re ripping fast flowy singletrack, putting the power down on punchy climbs, or tearing the tires off in the corners, the Optic continues to push the boundaries of what’s possible on a short travel trail bike. With increased rearward axle path, idler, and the innovative VPSHP suspension layout, this new design gives the Optic next-level confidence and capability, up or down the trail.\n\nShore Series – A limited-release, all-round beefier build, developed directly from experience our team has from pushing their own limits on local trails. We've stepped up on spec on our Shore Series bikes to help you handle more; a Fox 36 Performance Elite fork, 35mm rise bar, SRAM Maven brakes with metallic pads, Double Down rear tire casing, and Fox Float X2 rear shock to ride hard.\n\nLearn more about the Shore Series\n\nAll Optic models now include the One Up EDC lite tool to have you covered on the trail.",
